    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our undisputed anchor. With a score of 81.24 against Elder, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup and a premium #2 spot in the order, making him our highest-projected asset for both counting stats and the speed-dependent SB category. Following him, **Max Muncy** (71.26) provides immense value against a vulnerable Bradford; despite a minor penalty for the #7 spot, **Max Muncy**\u2019s power profile against left-handed pitching is too potent to fade. Meanwhile, **Josh Naylor** (64.62) and **Gabriel Moreno** (64.15) remain high-floor plays, as both capitalize on weak SP_xERA marks, with **Gabriel Moreno** specifically receiving a notable boost from his promotion to the #3 hole.\n\nPlatoon advantages are central to our construction today, specifically with **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 63.35 is driven by a +14% dynamic platoon bump against Tidwell. While we are monitoring the pending lineups for **Isaac Paredes**, **Cole Young**, and **Josh Naylor**, their projected spots remain favorable enough to command starts. **Jose Caballero** represents our most precarious play at 41.62; while he is vital for our speed-starved category, the daunting matchup against Cease forces a significant downward adjustment, keeping him on the periphery of our daily utility threshold.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the roster depth against our game cap management. While **Brice Turang** was considered for a middle-infield spot, his lack of a confirmed start today made him an easy exclusion in favor of **Travis Bazzana** (45.59), who offers a cleaner path to plate appearances. We continue to hold **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** in our reserves, keeping them ready should the current starters experience a downturn in efficiency. We remain sidelined regarding the long-term status of **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, whose continued presence on the IL forces us to squeeze maximum production from our active lineup to maintain our Roto standing.",
